        "original_id": "b4933782-d815-51f6-8b4e-01229c78b8e9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: William Gladstone Steel\n- Places: Crater Lake, Oregon, United States\n- Organizations: Crater Lake National Park\n- Concepts: creation of Crater Lake National Park, water clarity, deep blue color\n\nFacts:\n- William Gladstone Steel lived from September 7, 1854, to October 21, 1934.\n- William Gladstone Steel was called the \"father of Crater Lake\" for his role in the creation of Crater Lake National Park in Oregon, United States.\n- Crater Lake is the main feature of Crater Lake National Park.\n- Crater Lake is famous for its deep blue color and water clarity.",
